  "text": "**Step 1: Identify the terms**\n\nLet the five positive integers be represented as \\( a, b, c, d, e \\).\n\n**Step 2: Harmonic progression condition**\n\nThe first four terms \\( a, b, c, d \\) form a harmonic progression. For a sequence to be harmonic, the reciprocals must form an arithmetic progression. Therefore:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{b} - \\frac{1}{a} = \\frac{1}{c} - \\frac{1}{b} = \\frac{1}{d} - \\frac{1}{c}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Arithmetic progression condition**\n\nThe last four terms \\( b, c, d, e \\) form an arithmetic progression. Therefore:\n\\[\nc - b = d - c = e - d\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Difference between the first and last terms**\n\nGiven \\( e - a = 24 \\).\n\n**Step 5: Express terms in terms of \\( a \\)**\n\nFrom the arithmetic progression condition:\n\\[\nc = b + k, \\quad d = c + k = b + 2k, \\quad e = d + k = b + 3k\n\\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is the common difference.\n\n**Step 6: Substitute into the harmonic progression condition**\n\nFor the harmonic progression:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{b} - \\frac{1}{a} = \\frac{1}{c} - \\frac{1}{b}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{b} - \\frac{1}{a} = \\frac{1}{b + k} - \\frac{1}{b}\n\\]\nSolving this equation:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{b} - \\frac{1}{a} = -\\frac{k}{b(b + k)}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{b + k - a}{ab(b + k)} = -\\frac{k}{b(b + k)}\n\\]\n\\[\nb + k - a = -k\n\\]\n\\[\nb = a - 2k\n\\]\n\n**Step 7: Substitute \\( b \\) and \\( e \\) into the difference condition**\n\nThe difference \\( e - a = 24 \\):\n\\[\nb + 3k - a = 24\n\\]\nSubstitute \\( b = a - 2k \\):\n\\[\n(a - 2k) + 3k - a = 24\n\\]\n\\[\nk = 24\n\\]\n\n**Step 8: Find the terms**\n\nNow, \\( b = a - 2k = a - 48 \\).\n\nFrom the arithmetic progression:\n\\[\nc = b + k = a - 48 + 24 = a - 24\n\\]\n\\[\nd = c + k = a - 24 + 24 = a\n\\]\n\\[\ne = d + k = a + 24\n\\]\n\n**Step 9: Sum of the five terms**\n\n\\[\na + b + c + d + e = a + (a - 48) + (a - 24) + a + (a + 24) = 5a\n\\]\n\n**Step 10: Calculate \\( a \\) using \\( e - a = 24 \\)**\n\n\\[\n(a + 24) - a = 24\n\\]\nThis is consistent.\n\n**Final answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{240}\n\\]",
